 "section_summary": "This section (pages 483-534) comprises a continuous segment of an official roster of Japanese educational institutions located in Hokkaido Prefecture, specifically covering village and town elementary schools (Shoto Kyoiku). The listing contains institutional entries numbered 326 through 1,000, arranged alphabetically from Higashishikari Elementary School to Nibetsu Elementary School. For each institution, the table records the school name with English translation, administrative address (town/village and district), founding date, and disaggregated male, female, and total figures for student enrollments and teaching personnel as of April 30, 1946, and November 30, 1946.",
