   "summary": "This official roster tabulates elementary schools (numbered 326 through 1,000) located in villages and towns throughout Hokkaido Prefecture, arranged alphabetically from Higashishikari Elementary School to Nibetsu Elementary School. Each entry details the school's name, municipal and district jurisdiction, founding date, and comparative figures for male, female, and total student enrollments and teaching personnel as of April 30 and November 30, 1946. Occasional annotations specify branch schools included in administrative counts or record closures, such as the dissolution of Motoyama Elementary School in July 1946.",
